.TH TERM-NOTIFY-SOUND 1 "2026-10-23" "tmux-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
term-notify-sound \- emit a terminal-aware completion notification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B term-notify-sound
.RB [ \-\-owner
.IR pid ]
.RB [ \-\-exit-status
.IR code ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B term-notify-sound
plays a lightweight terminal notification by emitting one standard terminal
bell. The terminal client renders that bell, so local and remote-development
sessions use the same transport.
.PP
If
.I /dev/tty
is unavailable, the helper attempts to write to the current pane TTY.
.PP
Inside tmux, the helper also marks the pane that rang as pending with
.BR "term-pane-mark set pending" ,
which sets the pane user option
.B @term_notify_pending
to
.BR 1 .
tmux records a bell against a window, not the pane that rang it, so this
option is how a tmux configuration can show which pane wants attention. The
helper only sets the option; the configuration that renders it owns clearing
it, for example from
.B pane-focus-in
and
.B pane-focus-out
hooks.
.PP
When the bell goes straight to the controlling terminal,
.BR term-pane-mark (1)
decides which pane, if any, this process owns. When the bell falls back to the
pane's own pty, that pane is marked directly. The helper runs the
.B term-pane-mark
beside it, falling back to the one on
.BR PATH ;
a missing helper or a failed mark is ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-owner " pid"
Pass
.I pid
to the pending mark, which then lands only while that process runs in the
foreground of the pane's terminal; see
.BR term-pane-mark (1).
An agent's hook passes the agent, so a program the agent launched, which
inherits its pane but rings through the pane fallback without a terminal of
its own, cannot mark the agent's pane. The bell still rings.
.TP
.BI \-\-exit-status " code"
Pass a decimal shell exit status from 0 through 255 to the pending mark.
Options may appear in either order. Leading zeroes are accepted and removed.
A nonzero status publishes the pane option
.B @term_notify_exit_status
before marking the pane pending. A zero status or no status clears any stale
failure metadata. The terminal bell is unchanged; the tmux configuration
renders the status and clears it along with the pending mark when visited.
Status is accepted only through this option, not through the environment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM_NOTIFY_TTY
Override the primary terminal device, which defaults to
.IR /dev/tty .
The tmux pane TTY remains the fallback when this device cannot be opened.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The notification was emitted or intentionally ignored after best-effort
fallbacks.
.TP
.B 64
The arguments were invalid; nothing rang.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR term-pane-mark (1),
.BR tmux-copy-last-output (1)
